# TerrainFly environment template
# Copy to .env.local and fill in real values:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Rules:
# - Never commit .env.local
# - Never paste secret tokens, Garmin passwords, or OAuth secrets in git, chat, or the client
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are bundled into the browser. Only public, URL-restricted map tokens belong there.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# V1 REQUIRED — Mapbox (3D terrain + satellite / standard styles)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create at https://account.mapbox.com/access-tokens/
# Use a PUBLIC token only (starts with pk.). Do not put an sk. secret token here.
# Restrict the token URL to:
#   http://localhost:3000/*
#   http://127.0.0.1:3000/*
# Keep default public scopes (styles, fonts, datasets read). No secret scopes.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Optional style overrides. Defaults in code can use these Mapbox styles:
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_STYLE_SATELLITE=mapbox://styles/mapbox/standard-satellite
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_STYLE_STANDARD=mapbox://styles/mapbox/outdoors-v12
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TERRAIN_SOURCE=mapbox://mapbox.mapbox-terrain-dem-v1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# V1 OPTIONAL — MapLibre / MapTiler fallback (only if we skip Mapbox)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create at https://cloud.maptiler.com/account/keys/
# Restrict by HTTP origin. Public client key, not an admin key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# V1 OPTIONAL — CesiumJS path (only if we use Cesium instead of Mapbox GL)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create at https://ion.cesium.com/tokens
# Public scopes only: assets:read (and geocode if needed). Restrict by app URL.
# Do not enable assets:write, tokens:write, or other private scopes on a browser token.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CESIUM_ION_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# V3+ OPTIONAL — server-side export (not needed for V1 interactive viewer)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FFmpeg is a local binary, not an API key. Leave unset until video export.
# FFMPEG_PATH=/usr/local/bin/ffmpeg

# Object storage for rendered videos — not used in V1.
# S3_BUCKET=
# S3_REGION=
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LATER — Garmin Personal API (your own Connect data only)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create at https://connect.garmin.com/app/settings/personalApiToken
# Shown once. Treat like a password. Not for other users. Never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# GARMIN_PERSONAL_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# V4 ONLY — Garmin Connect Business / Starter (other users)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Apply as the company: https://www.garmin.com/en-US/forms/StarterGarminConnectDeveloperAccess/
# Overview: https://developer.garmin.com/gc-developer-program
# After approval, Garmin issues OAuth client id + secret.
# Never ask users for Garmin email/password. Never use unofficial Connect scrapers.
# Server-side only. Never prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# GARMIN_CLIENT_ID=
# GARMIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GARMIN_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/garmin/callback
